concept index {
  name     = "Index"
  summary  = "A curated collection of links that adds a top-level entry to the wskill's navigation — beyond the four units."
  related  = [datapresentation, concept]
  body {
    p <<BODY
      An index is how you add an item to the wskill's menu. The four unit kinds (concept,
      entity, fact, process) are gathered automatically, but an `index` lets you author a
      hand-curated page of links and have it appear as its own top-level entry — a chapter in
      the book's sidebar and a menu item in the skill.
    BODY

    p <<BODY
      Declare an `index` block with a `name` and a `body` of links; it renders to its own page
      and is listed at the top of the navigation. An index may nest child `index` blocks one
      level deep, which render indented under the parent — so a single index can group several
      related sub-pages under one menu heading.
    BODY
  }
}
